{"book":18,"chapter":18,"context":{"chapter":18,"title":"Bildad: The Wicked Man's Lamp","summary":"Bildad, offended at being treated like a beast, describes the downfall of the wicked: his lamp goes out, traps seize him, disease eats him and his name disappears from the earth.","background":"Bildad never names Job, but his portrait matches Job's losses closely: a ruined household, a body consumed by disease, no children left. The 'king of terrors' (v. 14) is death personified, and 'the firstborn of death' (v. 13) is probably a deadly disease. Brimstone scattered on his home (v. 15) recalls the judgment on Sodom.","customs":[{"term":"Hunting traps","verses":"18:8-10","note":"Bildad stacks up several Hebrew words for nets, snares, gins and nooses, the tools of a bird or animal hunter."}],"watchFor":["The lamp and light imagery at the start (vv. 5–6). Job answers it directly in 21:17.","How every detail quietly points at Job's own situation."],"connections":["Proverbs 13:9","Proverbs 24:20","Genesis 19:24","Psalms 109:13"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיַּעַן","vaiya'an","H6030","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he answered"],["בִּלְדַּד","bildad","H1085","HNpm","Bildad"],["הַשֻּׁחִי","hashuchi","H7747","HTd/Ngmsa","the Shuhite"],["וַיֹּאמַר","vaiyomar","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"]],"x":[[18002011,18002011,3],[18008001,18008001,3]],"xn":2},"2":{"w":[["עַד","'ad-","H5704","HR","until"],["אָנָה","'anah","H575","HTi","when?"],["תְּשִׂימוּן","tesimun","H7760","HVqi2mp/Sn","will you make !"],["קִנְצֵי","kintzei","H7078","HNcmpc","ends"],["לְמִלִּין","lemilin","H4405","HR/Ncmpa","of words"],["תָּבִינוּ","tavinu","H995","HVqi2mp","you will consider"],["וְאַחַר","ve'achar","H310","HC/Acmsa","and after"],["נְדַבֵּר","nedaber","H1696","HVpi1cp","we will speak"]],"x":[[18013005,18013006,3],[20018013,20018013,3]],"xn":2},"3":{"w":[["מַדּוּעַ","madua'","H4069","HTi","why?"],["נֶחְשַׁבְנוּ","nechshavnu","H2803","HVNp1cp","are we regarded"],["כַבְּהֵמָה","khabehemah","H929","HRd/Ncfsa","like <the> ca